        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function is used to swap the front and back buffers of a window when rendering, effectively displaying what has been rendered. The behavior of this function depends on the specific implementation of the OpenGL library being used.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>void</para>
</simplesect>
Swaps the front and back buffers of the specified window.</para>
<para>This function is used to swap the front and back buffers of a window when rendering, effectively displaying what has been rendered so far on the screen. The behavior of this function depends on the platform and graphics API being used. For example, it may not be necessary or possible to call this function at every frame. However, calling it once per frame ensures that the display is updated as quickly as possible. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
